For every finite $S\subset\mathbb Z$ and all real bounded compactly supported measurable functions $F_0,F_1,F_2$ on $\mathbb R_+^2$, $$\label{eq:main}
 \sum_{k\in S}\sum_{\mathbf I\in\mathcal A_k}
       \lvert L_{\mathbf I}(F_0,F_1,F_2)\rvert
 \le 40\prod_{v=0}^2\lVert F_v\rVert_{L^3(\mathbb R_+^2)}.$$

If $T\ge0$ and $U=U^*$ satisfy $-T\le U\le T$, then $U$ is supported on $T$ and $$\label{eq:gap}
 \frac{\Phi(T+U)+\Phi(T-U)}2-\Phi(T)
       \ge\frac{1}{2\sqrt2}b_T(U).$$

For the maps in <a href="#eq:row-star" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:row-star">[eq:row-star]</a>, let $D_v:H_v\to H_v$ be symmetric with $\lVert D_v\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\le1$, and put $U_v=R_v^*D_vR_v$. Then $U_v$ is supported on $T_v$, and $$\label{eq:trace}
 \lvert \mathop{\mathrm{tr}}(D_0W_0D_1W_1D_2W_2)\rvert
       \le\frac53\sum_{v=0}^2 b_{T_v}(U_v).$$ The constant is independent of all three dimensions.

For $\mathbf I\in\mathcal A_k$, $k\ge m+1$, define $$\delta(\mathbf I)
 =\frac14\sum_{\mathbf I'\in\operatorname{ch}(\mathbf I)}
                     e(\mathbf I')-e(\mathbf I).$$ Then $\delta(\mathbf I)\ge0$, and $$\label{eq:local-control}
 \lvert \tau(\mathbf I)\rvert
       \le\frac{10\sqrt2}{3}\,\delta(\mathbf I).$$

For the step functions of Section <a href="#sec:dyadic" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="sec:dyadic">4</a> and every $k\ge m$, set $$J_k=\sum_{\mathbf I\in\mathcal A_k}2^{2k}e(\mathbf I).$$ Then $$\label{eq:total}
 0\le J_k\le2\sqrt2\sum_{v=0}^2\lVert F_v\rVert_3^3.$$ For $k\ge m+1$, $$\label{eq:telescope}
 \sum_{\mathbf I\in\mathcal A_k}2^{2k}\delta(\mathbf I)
       =J_{k-1}-J_k.$$

For every $k\in\mathbb Z$ and real $F_v\in L^3(\mathbb R_+^2)$, $$\label{eq:one-scale}
 \sum_{\mathbf I\in\mathcal A_k}\lvert L_{\mathbf I}(F_0,F_1,F_2)\rvert
       \le\prod_{v=0}^2\lVert F_v\rVert_3.$$ Consequently the sequence $(L_{\mathbf I}(F_0,F_1,F_2))_{\mathbf I\in\mathcal A_k}$ depends continuously on the inputs as a map from $L^3\times L^3\times L^3$ to $\ell^1(\mathcal A_k)$.
